  "result": "I fixed it. The options themselves were listed in the right order. The problem was the names inside each option: they were sorted longest prefix first, so help showed `--mid, -m` instead of the usual `-m, --mid`.\n\nThe cause was `join_options` in `src/click/formatting.py:319`, which sorted with `reverse=True`. I removed that, so short flags like `-m` and `/x` now come before long ones like `--mid`.\n\n- **Before:** `--mid, -m TEXT`\n- **After:** `-m, --mid TEXT`\n\nThe test suite passes (1906 passed, 102 skipped, 1 expected failure). I haven't committed the change.",
